{"title":"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the two three-digit integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e164d77459e832afa1f8fa9a110628dfe5e06729.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{6A2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0ebd6e5d014d32206994f0fd2525d7577bffdeb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{B34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. What is the largest possible product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c43070a2acf8f4e25d98e48c404d9348a26d40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/9/09920c3af0daa12ac2ec5174e737c31e0f8cec75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{B}$\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A number is divisible by 18 iff it is divisible by 2 and 9. Divisibility by 2 is already satisfied, so we need the number to be divisible by 9; the divisibility rule for 9 states that we only need the sum of the digits to be divisible by 9. The units digit is 6; so the sum, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bbb2ef0bdc7856d0663a16bd268a8988a97ff0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = (6+b) \\cdot 10 + (A+3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" />, satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/0/2a04b26c640b9d1f975a012ada7d796183e445f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\equiv 3 \\pmod{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />. The only reasonable values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/8/d78f5d434cdbe2a4ef38ee9b763baf96c7857447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 3, 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d557e6ac5c4e99581af9f75190ed14123dbfd46.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} 6 &amp;&amp; A\\\\ + B &amp;&amp; 3  \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"74\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Casework\" title=\"Casework\">Casework</a>:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/6/f76720064e1b87e0398cffaa492648ca5ef307a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 3$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />. It quickly becomes apparent that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f779b42b919f0b9fda109e489a108eeb759c249.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 111$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />, which gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae1b11215392fd2731363d95198e4940a6da93c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 8, B = 4 (8,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/0/6b0237bc0a96a5c70e647aa80366c58b8921ecc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/d/c0dab39f9c471ec8ed61cd387c2f3d5722af8e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\ge 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e818d88a5e1b8c1b0984620bd48f15ae305992c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> gives either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/5/3552814dfdb20f6a4408498c7abd63b292d0ed44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 1, 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, and we carry over the one to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/a/51a646315f9faa55f1c23aba5e2f400997fe9fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. So the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b984d2a1f76bc936ab19412493dae4a8468f01d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 + B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> must add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae9eccf6d22d74be3e50d256d3a27d429d711292.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" />, which quickly shows us that this isn't possible.</li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/e/0fe7da0b98c469b78e6e9dbe63d2364b1ee6b632.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A &lt; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Greedy_algorithm\" title=\"Greedy algorithm\">Greedy algorithm</a>: if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/818297b710359102c7cd36d1ce433f64657cc77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 6$\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/06510f8514416859851faf3c518f83ca6b70cc6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + 3 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />, so the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/5/445f8edb20b26ceb3fcca63899221474f1cdf15f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> must be 12. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71b77af8e1a42cf61a2b5019c2eba72c061be9f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = 6 \\longrightarrow (6,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />. The other possible pairs are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/0/f7044ca0f50c3f8915247193e36fc8c413287630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5,7)(4,8)(3,9)(2,1)(1,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"200\" height=\"18\" />.</dd></dl>\n<p>Quickly taking the product of these, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47b1af246febb759b88a9817aaf2dc40775b6b75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6,6) \\Longrightarrow 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> gives us the largest product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC\" title=\"2005 PMWC\">2005 PMWC </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I14\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I14\">Problem I14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_T1\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem T1\">Problem T1</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\">I: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I1\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I2\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I3\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I4\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I5\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I6\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I7\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I8\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I9\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I10\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I11\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I12\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I13\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I14\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <br /> T: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_T1\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem T1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_T2\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem T2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_T3\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem T3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_T4\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem T4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_T5\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem T5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_T6\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem T6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_T7\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem T7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_T8\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem T8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_T9\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem T9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_T10\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem T10\">10</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017205801\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 198/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1656/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 126/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4989/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.206      1 Template:PMWC_box\n100.00%    7.206      1 -tota